<title>USA: DFS shareholder says LVMH reneged on purchase.</title>
<headline>DFS shareholder says LVMH reneged on purchase.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Robert Miller, owner of 38.75 percent of the DFS Group, said Wednesday that he expected to take legal action following the decision earlier today of LVMH Moet Hennessy Louis Vuitton to end negotiations to buy his stake in DFS.</p>
<p>In a statement, Miller charged that on Feb 3 LVMH had agreed in principle to acquire his shares in DFS and had reneged on that committment.  He said that as a result he would &quot;review all options and expect to take legal action.&quot;</p>
</text>
